    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0030" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control Austria/2–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-24T14:00:00+01:00">February 24,
                            1945—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 24—1:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1921. From Gray. I have heard that within recent weeks there have been
                    discussions in Washington concerning the preparation of an overall directive for
                    Austria based in large part on the original JCS 1067<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d15-f1"/> (which was designed to apply to Germany) and pointing
                    generally toward independent administration of the several zones. In view of the
                    fact that we have the basic PWC documents 217a and 218 on Austria<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d15-f2"/> and later material approved by the Department, it is
                    planned here as a matter of high priority to prepare a set of Austrian
                    directives incorporating in them the accepted general policies contained in the
                    above documents for Austria. We also have available the 16 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">15?</hi>] approved German directives,<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d15-f3"/> which can be used for guidance in preparing the Austrian
                    directives.</p>
                <p>I would appreciate being kept informed by telegram of the status of any
                    discussions in Washington on the matter of Austrian directives. [Gray.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d15-f1" n="60" xml:id="d15-f1-content">
                <p>Directive to SCAEF (Supreme Commander Allied Expeditionary Force) Regarding the
                    Military Government of Germany in the Period Immediately Following the Cessation
                    of Organized Resistance (Post Defeat), dated September 22, 1944, which was
                    circulated as a Joint Chiefs of Staff document designated J.C.S. 1067 dated
                    September 24, 1944. For text of the draft directive, see <ref
                        target="frus1945Malta#pg_143">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Conferences at Malta and Yalta</hi>, p.
                    143</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d15-f2" n="61" xml:id="d15-f2-content">
                <p>For texts, see <ref target="frus1944v01#pg_447">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1944, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 447</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus1944v01#pg_438">438</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d15-f3" n="62" xml:id="d15-f3-content">
                <p>See memorandum on p. 399 and especially footnote 87, <ref target="#pg402">p.
                        402</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
